    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug in the `frai gate init --ci` command. The issue was that the `--ci` flag was not being passed through to the `frai-gate` subprocess when called through the frai CLI.\n\n**The fix involved two changes to `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`:**\n\n1. **Enabled positional options on the parent program** (line 603):\n   - Added `.enablePositionalOptions()` to allow the `gate` subcommand to use `.passThroughOptions()`\n\n2. **Configured the gate command to pass through all options** (line 743):\n   - Added `.passThroughOptions()` to ensure the `--ci` flag is passed to the frai-gate subprocess\n   - Modified the action handler to accept both `args` and `options` parameters\n   - Reconstructed the command-line arguments by iterating through the options object and adding them back as flags\n\n**Testing:**\n- \u2705 `frai gate init --ci` now correctly creates both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n- \u2705 The rebuilt package was verified with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- \u2705 The generated workflow file contains the correct content",
